      },
      {
        "goal": "adler2::adler32_slice::Function",
        "id": "lane_add_execution",
        "kind": "lemma",
        "needs": [],
        "reason": "Each original nested loop iteration calls add_assign for a_vec and then b_vec. This rule checks all four array accesses and additions; the loop invariant must establish its per-lane overflow precondition.",
        "statement": "∀ (a b : ElicitGenerated.algo.U32X4), (∀ i : Fin 4, (a.val[i.val]'(by simpa using i.isLt)).val + (b.val[i.val]'(by simpa using i.isLt)).val ≤ Aeneas.Std.U32.max) → ElicitGenerated.algo.U32X4.Insts.CoreOpsArithAddAssignU32X4.add_assign a b ⦃ out => out.val.map (fun x => x.val) = List.zipWith (fun x y : Aeneas.Std.U32 => x.val + y.val) a.val b.val ⦄",
        "target": null,
        "theorem": "AdlerSpec.lane_add_spec"
      },
      {
        "goal": "adler2::adler32_slice::Function",
        "id": "inner_lane_loop",
        "kind": "lemma",
        "needs": [
          "lane_load",
          "lane_add_execution"
        ],
        "reason": "The outer chunk loop calls the original inner loop on at most 5552 four-byte chunks. This theorem proves termination, exact lane fold semantics and the per-iteration quadratic overflow bounds; its local count bound follows from the fixed 22208-byte chunk size, not a bound on the API input.",
        "statement": "∀ (cs : List (Aeneas.Std.Slice Aeneas.Std.U8)) (rem : Aeneas.Std.Slice Aeneas.Std.U8)\n    (a b : ElicitGenerated.algo.U32X4) (t : Nat)\n    (hlen : ∀ c ∈ cs, c.val.length = 4)\n    (ha : ∀ i, AdlerSpec.laneVal a i ≤ AdlerSpec.aBound t)\n    (hb : ∀ i, AdlerSpec.laneVal b i ≤ AdlerSpec.bBound t)\n    (ht : t + cs.length ≤ 5552),\n    ElicitGenerated.algo.Adler32.compute_loop0_loop0 { chunks := cs, remainder := rem } a b ⦃ out =>\n      (AdlerSpec.vals out.1, AdlerSpec.vals out.2) = AdlerSpec.laneModel (AdlerSpec.vals a, AdlerSpec.vals b) cs ∧\n      (∀ i, AdlerSpec.laneVal out.1 i ≤ AdlerSpec.aBound (t + cs.length)) ∧\n      (∀ i, AdlerSpec.laneVal out.2 i ≤ AdlerSpec.bBound (t + cs.length)) ⦄",
        "target": null,
        "theorem": "AdlerSpec.inner_loop"
      },
      {
        "goal": "adler2::adler32_slice::Function",
        "id": "outer_chunk_loop",
        "kind": "lemma",
        "needs": [
          "inner_lane_loop",
          "chunks_exact_execution"
        ],
        "reason": "The compute caller stops at compute_loop0. This theorem covers any number of full 22208-byte chunks, reconstructs every chunk from four-byte pieces, checks the inner loop and original modulo helpers, and proves the exact fold of reduced lane and scalar states with preserved machine bounds.",
        "statement": "∀ (cs : List (Aeneas.Std.Slice Aeneas.Std.U8)) (rem : Aeneas.Std.Slice Aeneas.Std.U8)\n    (a b : Aeneas.Std.U32) (av bv : ElicitGenerated.algo.U32X4)\n    (hlen : ∀ c ∈ cs, c.val.length = 22208) (ha : a.val ≤ 65535) (hb : b.val ≤ 65535)\n    (hav : ∀ i, AdlerSpec.laneVal av i ≤ 65520) (hbv : ∀ i, AdlerSpec.laneVal bv i ≤ 65520),\n    ElicitGenerated.algo.Adler32.compute_loop0 22208#usize {chunks := cs, remainder := rem} a b av bv ⦃ out =>\n      ∃ groups : List (List (Aeneas.Std.Slice Aeneas.Std.U8)),\n        List.Forall₂ AdlerSpec.blockRep groups cs ∧\n        (out.1.val, AdlerSpec.vals out.2.1, AdlerSpec.vals out.2.2) = groups.foldl (AdlerSpec.outerStep a.val) (b.val, AdlerSpec.vals av, AdlerSpec.vals bv) ∧\n        out.1.val ≤ 65535 ∧\n        (∀ i, AdlerSpec.laneVal out.2.1 i ≤ 65520) ∧ (∀ i, AdlerSpec.laneVal out.2.2 i ≤ 65520) ⦄",
        "target": null,
        "theorem": "AdlerSpec.outer_loop"
      },
      {
        "goal": "adler2::adler32_slice::Function",
        "id": "final_lane_loop",
        "kind": "lemma",
        "needs": [
          "inner_lane_loop"
        ],
        "reason": "Covers the original final partial-chunk loop using the checked identical inner-loop body, with exact lane recurrence and internal arithmetic bounds.",
        "statement": "∀ (cs : List (Aeneas.Std.Slice Aeneas.Std.U8)) (rem : Aeneas.Std.Slice Aeneas.Std.U8)\n    (a b : ElicitGenerated.algo.U32X4) (t : Nat)\n    (hlen : ∀ c ∈ cs, c.val.length = 4)\n    (ha : ∀ i, AdlerSpec.laneVal a i ≤ AdlerSpec.aBound t)\n    (hb : ∀ i, AdlerSpec.laneVal b i ≤ AdlerSpec.bBound t)\n    (ht : t + cs.length ≤ 5552),\n    ElicitGenerated.algo.Adler32.compute_loop1 { chunks := cs, remainder := rem } a b ⦃ out =>\n      (AdlerSpec.vals out.1, AdlerSpec.vals out.2) = AdlerSpec.laneModel (AdlerSpec.vals a, AdlerSpec.vals b) cs ∧\n      (∀ i, AdlerSpec.laneVal out.1 i ≤ AdlerSpec.aBound (t + cs.length)) ∧\n      (∀ i, AdlerSpec.laneVal out.2 i ≤ AdlerSpec.bBound (t + cs.length)) ⦄",
        "target": null,
